        "original_id": "271ca359-e158-52f5-bbe7-2629238826fd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Isaac Newton, Albert Einstein\n- Concepts: classical theory of gravity, inertia, circular motion, straight-line motion, deficiency in Newton's theory, photoelectric effect, quantum theory\n- Awards: 1921 Nobel Prize in Physics\n\nFacts:\n- Isaac Newton's classical theory of gravity says that without gravity the planets would immediately stop moving in circular motion and, due to inertia, would travel in a straight line.\n- Albert Einstein identified a deficiency in Isaac Newton's theory of gravity.\n- Albert Einstein received the 1921 Nobel Prize in Physics for his services to theoretical physics and especially for discovering the law of the photoelectric effect, which was a pivotal step in the evolution of quantum theory.",
